<title>SPAIN: Spain's Feb trade deficit at 243.6 bln pta. [CORRECTED 12:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>Spain's Feb trade deficit at 243.6 bln pta. [CORRECTED 12:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The customs department of the Economy Ministry gave the following figures (billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE		FEB 97	JAN 97	 FEB 96</p>
<p> Exports		     1,079.2     1,079.4	 994.8</p>
<p> Imports		     1,322.9     1,188.5     1,232.5</p>
<p> Deficit/surplus	    -243.6	-109.1	-237.7</p>
<p> Def/surplus yr to date   -352.8	-109.1	-411.0</p>
<p>(Corrects deficit in year to Feb '97).</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures are customs-cleared data. The January data are the provisional ones, originally reported.</p>
<p>The following is the trade data with the European Union.</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE (EU)     FEB 97	  JAN 97	FEB 96</p>
<p> Exports		    773.5	   777.2	  737.4</p>
<p> Imports		    872.0	   737.8	  789.6</p>
<p> Deficit/surplus	  -98.4	    39.3	  -52.2</p>
<p> Def/surplus yr to date -59.0	    39.3	  -42.4</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
